  "id": "COMPOUND:42907 - PROTEIN:2718",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Bakuchalcone may interact with Triosephosphate isomerase through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Bakuchalcone to the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 zeta chain, which is targeted by N-Hydroxyannomontine, and N-Hydroxyannomontine is also targeted by Triosephosphate isomerase. This indicates a potential regulatory role of Bakuchalcone in the activity of CD3 zeta chain, which in turn influences the activity of Triosephosphate isomerase. The second and third pathways show that Bakuchalcone targets Integrin alpha-4 and Complement C5, both of which are also targeted by the same compound, and both of which are ultimately targeted by Triosephosphate isomerase. These findings suggest that Bakuchalcone may exert its effects through a network of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the modulation of Triosephosphate isomerase activity. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Bakuchalcone influences downstream targets that are involved in the regulation of Triosephosphate isomerase, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
